WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.650
Deep inside a handheld game
sits a tiny 8-bit processor.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.290
It can add and move bits, but it
has no circuit for multiplying.

3
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.900
Now the player clears a level,
and the game needs a bonus score:

4
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.010
22 times 8.

5
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:19.210
So how can it multiply by 8
without doing any multiplying?

6
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.310
In this mission, you'll see that every
binary column is worth double the one on

7
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.450
its right.

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.030
You'll learn the binary shift, which slides
every bit along the register and fills

9
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.730
the gaps with zeros.

10
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.730
And you'll see what happens
to bits pushed off the end.

11
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.090
They're lost.

12
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.480
Your mission: work out how a computer can
multiply by 8 without ever multiplying.
